# Same range cuts as the DC3/DC4 sources (optimizes sim time):
DefaultRangeCut 0.005
Region Spacecraft
Spacecraft.Volume SCbody
Spacecraft.RangeCut 1.

Region Pipebody
Pipebody.Volume PIPbody
Pipebody.RangeCut 1.

DetectorTimeConstant 0.000002

# Local particle event: quasi-trapped electrons, exp(-E/200 keV),
# peak I(>30 keV) = 27 e/cm2/s/sr at 90 deg pitch, sin^4 pitch-angle distribution.
# Rocking -21.88 deg, yaw 14.49 deg, field dip 0 deg. Directions in detector frame.
DataChallenge.Source E_LOCLPAR0015
E_LOCLPAR0015.ParticleType 3
E_LOCLPAR0015.Beam FarFieldNormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction E_LOCLPAR0015_beam.dat
E_LOCLPAR0015.Spectrum NormalizedEnergyBeamFluxFunction
# Light-curve times are relative to t_ref = 1835583336.0 (unix s, first orientation row of this burst).
# Simulate with DC3_final_530km_3_month_with_slew_1sbins_GalacticEarth_cut_normed.ori and add t_ref to the simulated times afterwards.
# Original light curve (absolute unix times): E_LOCLPAR0015_lightcurve.dat; see sim_time_reference.txt.
E_LOCLPAR0015.Lightcurve File false E_LOCLPAR0015_lightcurve_shifted.dat
